        truths: ("{DL} bought the stamp used on the letter, and the handwriting on the envelope matches {D.him}.", "The letter itself was typed on a library printer anyone could use, and only the envelope resembles {DL}'s writing."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you write or mail that letter?", "\"No, I did not. I never wrote a demand to {V}, and I never sent anything to {V.him}.\""), .direct("Why would the envelope look like your handwriting?", "\"I don't know. Someone may have copied it. My handwriting is common, and I've signed lots of things that others could study.\""), .direct("Where was the letter typed?", "\"At a public library, as far as I can tell. The deputies told me the printer was open to anyone with a card.\""), .direct("Did you buy the stamp?", "\"I buy stamps all the time, and I may have sold or given some away. I can't say I bought that one.\""), .direct("What did you do when deputies told you about it?", "\"I told them it wasn't me. I gave them handwriting samples, and I answered every question.\""), .direct("How do you feel about the accusation?", "\"Angry and upset. I've been in court before, and I know it looks worse because of that.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, I was. I'm not proud of it, but I didn't write this.\""), .cross("You had a falling out with {V}, didn't you?", "\"We disagreed about something. I would not have blackmailed anyone over it.\""), .cross("The examiner says the handwriting matches, doesn't the examiner?", "\"That's what I've been told. I think someone copied it.\""), .cross("You can't name who forged your handwriting, can you?", "\"No, I can't. I wish I could.\""), .cross("You knew about the private information in the letter, didn't you?", "\"I knew some of it was talked about. I never used it.\"")],
