        truths: ("The motor was running and {DL} was at the wheel when the marine officer boarded.", "The boat was anchored with the engine off, and a sober friend was at the helm before the officer came alongside."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were you operating the boat?", "\"No. The boat was anchored with the engine off when the officer came, and my friend was at the wheel.\""), .direct("Why were you at the wheel when the officer arrived?", "\"I'd stepped to the wheel to move a cooler, and my friend was driving. The officer came alongside as I stood there.\""), .direct("Had you been drinking?", "\"I'd had a couple of beers, and I'm not hiding that. My friend had not.\""), .direct("Why did you say you'd had a couple of drinks?", "\"Because it was true. I didn't think having a drink on a boat that wasn't moving was a problem.\""), .direct("What did you tell the officer about the engine?", "\"That it had been off for a while. A friend can tell you the same thing.\""), .direct("How did you get back to the ramp?", "\"My friend drove the boat back, with the officer following. I rode along.\""), .cross("You have been in this court before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I know better than to drive impaired. I wasn't driving.\""), .cross("Your test was 0.09, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. I was a bit over the line, and I'm sorry for that.\""), .cross("The officer heard the motor running, didn't he?", "\"{OFF.He} says so. I believe it was running when we started it again.\""), .cross("Your friend isn't here to testify, is he?", "\"No. I hope my friend can be heard.\""), .cross("You were standing at the wheel when the officer boarded, weren't you?", "\"Yes, but I wasn't steering.\"")],
        openings: ("A marine patrol officer stopped a boat on the lake and found {D} at the wheel with the motor running. A breath test read 0.09, and {DL} had been in this court before on {PRIOR}. The State will show the officer's report and the test.", "The boat was anchored with the engine off, and a sober friend was at the helm. A person on a boat adrift on a calm afternoon is not operating it, and the breath test says nothing about who was driving."),
        closings: ("The officer found {D} at the wheel with the motor running and a breath test of 0.09. {DL} had been here in {PRIORDATE}. That is operating a vessel while impaired.", "The boat was anchored, the engine was off, and a sober friend was at the helm. The State cannot prove {D} was operating a boat that was sitting still."),
        timeline: [(0, "A marine patrol officer approaches a boat on the lake."), (0, "The officer finds {D} at the wheel and boards."), (0, "A breath test reads 0.09.")],
        identified: "Breath Test",
        mood: .wantsConviction)

